    "The startup variables have only upper bounds (startup <= n, <= available, <= n in the previous period) and no lower-bound link such as startup[t,p] >= n[t,p] - n[t,p-1]. The solver can therefore set every startup to 0 and pay no startup cost, even though generators go from off to on.",
