    "The constraint startup[t,p] <= n[t,p-1] has no meaning as a startup rule. It limits startups by the previous period's active count rather than counting new activations."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The model uses available = max_active (1 Type 0, 2 Type 1) as the number of generators available."
  ],
  "reason": "The model never forces startups to be counted, so startup costs are omitted and the optimal value is understated."
